### Linux Attack Analysis:
- Hash Format: SHA-512 with salt + 5000 iterations (v = SHA-512^5000(password||salt))
- Targets: root, Morpheus, Neo, Trinity, Cypher, Smith, Cobb, Arthur (8 users)
- Total Runtime: 25 minutes across 3 strategic phases
- Resource Management: Successfully avoided system overheating
- Success Rate: 0/8 passwords (0%) - validates computational security design
- Computational Complexity: 5000x more expensive than NTLM per password guess
- Security Validation: Demonstrates effectiveness of salt + iteration count design

